- op: create  # df2b
  at: '2026-10-03T13:18:05Z'  # df2b
  by: agent  # df2b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df2b
  clock: 1  # df2b
  nonce: df2b  # df2b
  data:  # df2b
    kind: work_item  # df2b
    title: "python: a write into a caller-supplied object (json.dump, pickle.dump, csv writer methods) is fs_write even when the object is an in-memory io.StringIO; Go's in_memory io_target_kind has no python twin"  # df2b
    status: todo_hard  # df2b
    priority: 3  # df2b
    parent:  # df2b
    tags: []  # df2b
    isbefore: []  # df2b
    duplicate_of: []  # df2b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # df2b
    pr_ref:  # df2b
    description: "FOUND BY WI-kozaj (2026-10-03) while A/B-ing the csv write rows on pretix. NOT introduced by WI-kozaj: the same shape held before it, one call earlier.\n\npython.yaml rows a write INTO a caller-supplied object as fs_write: json.dump, pickle.dump, and (WI-kozaj) _csv.Writer.writerow/writerows and csv.DictWriter.writerow/writerows/writeheader. The row is right when the object is a file the caller opened. It is a vacuous host_fs sink when the object is an in-memory buffer. Observed on real code, analyzer output read back to source: pretix src/pretix/control/views/vouchers.py:116 and src/pretix/control/views/waitinglist.py:322 build `output = io.StringIO()` and then `csv.writer(output, ...)` / `writer.writerow(...)`; both arms of WI-kozaj's A/B classify that write fs_write (arm A at defusedcsv.csv.writer, arm B at defusedcsv.csv._ProxyWriter.writerow). No pretix verdict moved on it (the generic claims found no flow into these sites), so the cost measured so far is zero findings; it is a precision exposure, not a measured false positive.\n\nGo already solves the twin: io_target_kind is stamped from the writer argument's last binding, and an in_memory target (bytes.Buffer, strings.Builder) is refused by the carry gate (WI-suhug, test_sink_match_reads_the_writer.py::test_an_in_memory_writer_is_no_sink). Python has no such stamp. Proposed shape, not decided: resolve the file-object argument (or, for a writer type, the argument its factory was called with) to its binding and stamp in_memory for io.StringIO / io.BytesIO. NOT CHECKED: how many corpus sites write json/pickle/csv into an in-memory buffer; whether any verdict anywhere depends on one."  # df2b
    fields: {}  # df2b
- op: discuss  # 43e7
  at: '2026-10-03T17:38:19Z'  # 43e7
  by: agent  # 43e7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 43e7
  clock: 2  # 43e7
  nonce: '43e7'  # 43e7
  message: "CORROBORATION from WI-vafad tranche 3 (2026-10-03, docs/audits/0022). Blind source-reading workers who never saw the catalogue notes returned UNDECIDABLE_BY_ARGUMENT 2/2 on all 8 python writer rows this item names that were in the sweep: csv.DictWriter writerow / writerows / writeheader, defusedcsv.csv.DictWriter writerow / writerows / writeheader, and defusedcsv.csv._ProxyWriter writerow / writerows. Each worker independently cited the caller-supplied file-like object as what decides the destination (file, pipe, StringIO, stdout). _csv.Writer.writerow / writerows came back UNREADABLE (C-implemented). No new finding, but the item's premise was reproduced from source by two independent readers."  # 43e7
- op: discuss  # 98a0
  at: '2026-11-01T10:55:51Z'  # 98a0
  by: agent  # 98a0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 98a0
  clock: 3  # 98a0
  nonce: 98a0  # 98a0
  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/misc1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. Fixture json.dump/pickle.dump/csv.writer(...).writerow into io.StringIO/BytesIO: io-boundaries reports all as fs_write, with meta.io_target_kind=None. Python now has io_target_kind stamping (WI-himim 8e124fa862, py.py _STREAM_FACTORY_MEDIA) but only for asyncio stream-factory receivers (net_stream/pipe); there is no in_memory medium and no argument-binding stamp, so the item stands and can reuse that machinery. MECHANISM: python stamps io_target_kind only from stream-factory receivers, never from the file-object argument binding (no in_memory). SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-lasih."  # 98a0
